/-
  The badge `verify`'s per-entry module (TRUSTED harness code; rendered per entry by
  `harness/evaluate.py`, which replaces `{{solution_module}}`). It is the wiring and nothing else:
  the badge's code (the file parser, the hex parser, the timer, the command line) is
  `RecursionFast/Badge.lean`, compiled before the entry existed, without the entry's instances
  and notations in scope. This module is elaborated with them in scope, so it must hold nothing
  but this one definition: no arithmetic, parsing, string or hex code. The gate checks after the
  build that it declares `main` alone, with the value `RFBadge.main
  RecursionFast.Challenge.submission`, and no attribute (`Gate.lean`, `--wiring`).
-/
import {{solution_module}}
import RecursionFast.Badge

def main : List String → IO UInt32 := RFBadge.main RecursionFast.Challenge.submission
